---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Recommendation Blocks — Case Study"
  description="Built product recommendations from zero to 80%+ adoption across five regions by designing trust-building three-tier ladder: Manual → Automated → Smart."
>
  <article style="padding: 52px 0;">
    <nav style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
      <a href="/case-studies" style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none;">← Back to case studies</a>
    </nav>

    <div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 24px;">
      <h1 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: var(--fs-32); font-weight: 600; margin: 0; flex: 1;">Recommendation Blocks</h1>
      <button onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText(window.location.href); this.textContent='Copied!'; setTimeout(() => this.textContent='Copy link', 2000);" style="padding: 8px 16px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: transparent; cursor: pointer; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent); white-space: nowrap; border-radius: 3px; transition: all 0.2s ease;" onmouseenter="this.style.borderColor='var(--accent)'" onmouseleave="this.style.borderColor='var(--rule)'">Copy link</button>
    </div>

    <p style="font-size: 16px; color: var(--ink-2); margin-bottom: 32px; max-width: 65ch;">I built the company's product recommendation system from zero. Solved cold-start by tiering on data requirements: three independent engines, each deployable when its data dependency is met. Multi-region serving under latency SLA.</p>

    <div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 32px;">
      <span style="background: var(--accent-wash); color: var(--accent); padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 13px;">day-1 deployment · no data required</span>
      <span style="background: var(--accent-wash); color: var(--accent); padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 13px;">5 regions · 200ms p99</span>
      <span style="background: var(--accent-wash); color: var(--accent); padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 13px;">built on the platform ↑</span>
    </div>

    <p style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-3); margin-bottom: 40px;">Node.js · Redis · MongoDB Atlas (multi-region) · ClickHouse · Google Pub/Sub</p>

    <!-- My Role -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 24px;">My Role</h2>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">What I personally owned</h3>
        <div style="display: grid; gap: 12px; max-width: 65ch;">
          <div><strong>Product architecture</strong> — designed three-tier trust model (Manual/Automated/Smart) to reduce merchant risk and enable gradual adoption</div>
          <div><strong>System design</strong> — architected multi-region serving, latency SLAs, and real-time ranking engine</div>
          <div><strong>Core implementation</strong> — architected and directed the Redis-backed live tier, MongoDB serving layer, and ranking algorithm; a small team (2–3 engineers) built and scaled it while I stayed close to product decisions and tradeoffs</div>
          <div><strong>Adoption strategy</strong> — worked with sales/success to position tiers, built tier progression measurement and ROI tracking</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">What the product achieved</h3>
        <div style="display: grid; gap: 12px; max-width: 65ch;">
          <div><strong>80%+ Smart-tier adoption</strong> — among merchants who trialled the tier</div>
          <div><strong>Multi-region latency</strong> — 200ms p99 across five regions with real-time ranking</div>
          <div><strong>Merchant trust</strong> — low-friction trust ladder moved from "risky feature" to default-on</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Context -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Context</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch;">ConvertCart serves 200+ merchants across five regions. Merchants are SMBs with low transaction volume on day 1. Recommendation systems require behavioral data to produce quality results. Architecture challenge: ship day 1 with zero data, scale to algorithmic sophistication as data accumulates. Multi-region serving introduces latency constraints.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Problem -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Problem</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin-bottom: 24px;">New merchant on day 1: zero behavioral data. Live recommendation ranking needs statistical significance to produce quality results. Ship live ranking immediately and recommendations are garbage—merchants disable the feature. By day 30 when data exists, trust is already destroyed. Cannot recover.</p>

      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin-bottom: 24px;">Architectural constraint: you need immediate value (day 1) with zero data, then scale to algorithmic sophistication as data accumulates. Cannot ship confident recommendations without data. Cannot gather data unless merchants use recommendations. Bootstrap problem.</p>

      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 32px; margin-top: 24px;">
        <div style="padding: 20px; background: var(--panel); border-radius: 4px;">
          <div style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">NAIVE APPROACH</div>
          <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;">
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">Ship live ranking day 1</li>
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">Trains on zero data</li>
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink);">Produces noise → merchants distrust system</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div style="padding: 20px; background: var(--panel); border-radius: 4px;">
          <div style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">ARCHITECTURAL CHALLENGE</div>
          <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;">
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">Immediate value, zero data required</li>
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">Bootstrap into sophisticated algorithms</li>
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink);">Serve multi-region under 200ms latency</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Architecture -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Architecture</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin-bottom: 24px;">Three independent engines, tiered on data requirements. Curated: CSM hand-picks, zero data, day 1. Automated: pattern rules, ~50 transactions (week 1), batch-refreshed. Smart: live behavioral ranking, 30+ days history + 500 orders + 200 unique customers (week 3-4), Redis-backed. Each tier deployable when its data threshold is met. Multi-region MongoDB for serving, ClickHouse for analytics.</p>

      <!-- Recommendation Architecture SVG -->
      <svg viewBox="0 0 640 480" style="max-width: 65ch; width: 100%; margin-bottom: 24px; display: block;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <defs>
          <style>
            .rec-box { fill: var(--panel); stroke: var(--rule-2); stroke-width: 1.5; }
            .rec-label { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; fill: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
            .rec-label-small { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; fill: var(--ink-2); }
            .rec-arrow { stroke: var(--ink-3); stroke-width: 2; fill: none; marker-end: url(#rec-arrowhead); }
          </style>
          <marker id="rec-arrowhead" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="9" refY="3" orient="auto">
            <polygon points="0 0, 10 3, 0 6" fill="var(--ink-3)" />
          </marker>
        </defs>

        <!-- Tier progression (left column) -->
        <text class="rec-label" x="100" y="25" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent);">TIER PROGRESSION</text>
        <rect class="rec-box" x="20" y="40" width="160" height="60" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label" x="100" y="65" text-anchor="middle">Manual</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="85" text-anchor="middle">CSM hand-picks</text>
        <line class="rec-arrow" x1="100" y1="100" x2="100" y2="130"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="125" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent);">trust ↑</text>

        <rect class="rec-box" x="20" y="130" width="160" height="60" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label" x="100" y="155" text-anchor="middle">Automated</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="175" text-anchor="middle">Rules · batch</text>
        <line class="rec-arrow" x1="100" y1="190" x2="100" y2="220"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="215" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent);">trust ↑</text>

        <rect class="rec-box" x="20" y="220" width="160" height="80" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label" x="100" y="250" text-anchor="middle">Smart</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="270" text-anchor="middle">(80%+ merchants)</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="285" text-anchor="middle">Live ranking · Redis</text>

        <!-- Multi-region serving (right column) -->
        <text class="rec-label" x="500" y="25" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent);">SERVING</text>
        <rect class="rec-box" x="420" y="40" width="160" height="50" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="500" y="70" text-anchor="middle">US · EU · APAC</text>

        <rect class="rec-box" x="420" y="100" width="160" height="50" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="500" y="130" text-anchor="middle">India · Brazil</text>

        <rect class="rec-box" x="420" y="160" width="160" height="60" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="500" y="185" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent); font-weight: 600;">200ms p99</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="500" y="205" text-anchor="middle">latency SLA</text>

        <!-- Latency tradeoff annotation -->
        <line style="stroke: var(--rule); stroke-width: 1;" x1="40" y1="340" x2="600" y2="340"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="320" y="360" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--ink-3);">Latency-freshness tradeoff: read replicas lag 5–10s, acceptable for merchant UX</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="320" y="380" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--ink-3);">Redis replication lag reduces on slow replica (fallback to cached tier), prioritizes speed over freshness</text>
      </svg>
    </section>

    <!-- Key Decisions -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Key Decisions</h2>
      <ol style="max-width: 65ch; list-style: none; padding: 0;">
        <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 20px;">
          <strong>Three independent engines tiered on data requirements</strong><br/>
          <span style="color: var(--ink-2);">Do not ship all tiers day 1. Tier deployment is blocked by data availability. Curated activates immediately (no data needed). Automated activates week 1-2 (50+ transactions). Smart activates week 3-4 (30+ days baseline). Each tier unblocks the next by generating data.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 20px;">
          <strong>Computation matched to data maturity</strong><br/>
          <span style="color: var(--ink-2);">Curated is static (no computation). Automated is batch rules (frequency > threshold). Smart is live ranking (statistical model). Cannot compute live ranking on day-7 data; would overfit.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 20px;">
          <strong>Redis-first serving, accept eventual consistency</strong><br/>
          <span style="color: var(--ink-2);">In-flight ranking state lost on Redis failure is acceptable for recommendations. Would not accept this for transactional orders. Latency requirement (200ms p99) demands in-memory serving.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink);">
          <strong>Read replicas trade freshness for latency across regions</strong><br/>
          <span style="color: var(--ink-2);">Serving from regional replicas incurs 5-10s replication lag. Acceptable cost for 200ms p99 serving. Alternative: central Redis for all regions means 300-500ms network latency. Chose lower latency.</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- Execution -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Execution</h2>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">Data Threshold Gating</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0;">Automated tier: monitored order volume. Gated at 50 cumulative transactions. Batch job runs daily; queries only fire once gate passes. Smart tier: monitored 30-day history, order count (≥500), unique customer count (≥200). Model retraining scheduled only after all thresholds met.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">Multi-Region Serving Under Latency SLA</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0;">Target: 200ms p99 across five regions (US, EU, APAC, India, Brazil). Deployed MongoDB instances in each region. Redis ranking cache replicated to regional instances with 5-10s lag. On replica lag, served cached tier (fallback to Automated) instead of blocking. Prioritized latency over freshness.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">Model Validation Before Deploy</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0;">Smart ranking trained on historical data. Before serving live, validated against held-out test sets. Checked for cardinality issues (one customer type over-indexed), signal stability (weights don't swing per retraining), and tail behavior (edge cases don't rank anomalously). Rejected models that failed validation.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">Monitoring & Rollback</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0;">Tracked block click-through rate and block latency per tier. Anomalies (CTR drop >10%, latency spike) paged on-call. Could disable tiers independently if quality degraded. Built canary deployment for Smart tier: new model runs on 5% of traffic first, compared metrics to incumbent.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Impact -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Impact</h2>

      <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 32px; padding: 32px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);">
        <div style="font-size: var(--fs-56); font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">200ms P99 · DAY 1</div>
        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0 auto;">Deployed Curated recommendations on day 1 across five regions under latency SLA</div>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">Technical Achievement</h3>
        <ul style="max-width: 65ch; list-style: none; padding: 0;">
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 12px;">Solved cold-start by tiering on data requirements. Zero data (Curated) → week 1 data (Automated) → week 4 data (Smart). Each tier deployable independently.</li>
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 12px;">Multi-region serving with regional Redis + fallback caching. 200ms p99 latency across five regions despite 5-10s replication lag.</li>
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 12px;">Model validation gate ensured Smart tier only served high-confidence rankings. Prevented garbage output from ruining system trust.</li>
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink);">Canary deployment pattern for ranking updates. New models validated on 5% traffic before full rollout.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">Scale</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0;">Day-1 deployment (zero data needed) · five regions · 200ms p99 latency target · three-tier architecture supports 30-day progression from Curated → Automated → Smart</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What I'd Change Today -->
    <section>
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">What I'd Change Today</h2>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">What I'd Preserve</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0;">Three-tier tiered-on-data-requirements model. Data dependencies block tier activation. This architecture prevented shipping garbage output and losing merchant trust on day 1.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">What I'd Change</h3>
        <ul style="max-width: 65ch; list-style: none; padding: 0;">
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Canary deployments from day one.</strong> Built it later, but early validation would have caught model quality issues faster.</li>
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Feature flag for Smart tier per merchant.</strong> All-or-nothing rollout was risky. Gradual merchant cohort rollout would allow faster issue detection.</li>
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink);">​<strong>Separate model retraining from serving.</strong> Current design retrains synchronously, risks latency spikes. Async retraining into separate cache layer would decouple.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section style="padding: 52px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); margin-top: 52px;">
      <p style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 16px;">Next steps</p>
      <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;">→ <a href="/case-studies/hard-problems" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none;">See production incidents that shaped this design</a></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;">→ <a href="/resume" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none;">Download my resume</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .case-next { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; padding-top: 32px; margin-top: 48px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
</style>
